	(text "T201 (SMPS.md): W1 primary, W2 aux, S1 shield and W3 heater in chamber B;\nW4/W5 (+S2) in chamber A on M1, W6/W7 (+S3) in chamber C on M2.\nAll secondaries triple-insulated wire. Core strapped to PE.\nW5/W7 feed the existing bias rectifiers D5/D6 (UF4007) on the amp sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 243.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c1cc2215-3409-4fd9-93fa-0ec2d0059b80")
	)
	(text "Bank M1: W4 -> A2 / G1, referenced to M1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 29.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2e3d525b-ccc5-4c2e-89eb-f0a41ac5837d")
	)
	(text "R202: 2x 110k 1W, R203: 3x 4M7 HV, C203: MKP, R104: 2x 68k 3W, R205: 2x 220k. Q201: insulated TO-220FP on the heatsink, equal pads on both banks.\nCap multiplier: Q201 follows the gate filter R202/R203/C203 (tau ~1.5 s), drop ~7 V + Vgs ~ 11 V, removes the 100 Hz bus ripple and the switching residue.\nB+ delay: U201 (monostable, 1.1 x R206 x C205 ~ 52 s from power-on) drives Q202, which holds the gate filter at M1. The bias rail comes up at once.\nC208: optional Y-cap to BUS- (DNP), fit only with its twin on the other bank, both equal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a49ca3a2-fc25-4876-b876-00b7d75929d3")
	)
	(text "Bank M2: W6 -> A1 / G2, referenced to M2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 151.13 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "47b32380-7aa2-43fe-8708-845558738d85")
	)
	(text "R222: 2x 110k 1W, R223: 3x 4M7 HV, C223: MKP, R102: 2x 68k 3W, R225: 2x 220k. Q221: insulated TO-220FP on the heatsink, equal pads on both banks.\nCap multiplier: Q221 follows the gate filter R222/R223/C223 (tau ~1.5 s), drop ~7 V + Vgs ~ 11 V, removes the 100 Hz bus ripple and the switching residue.\nB+ delay: U221 (monostable, 1.1 x R226 x C225 ~ 52 s from power-on) drives Q222, which holds the gate filter at M2. The bias rail comes up at once.\nC228: optional Y-cap to BUS- (DNP), fit only with its twin on the other bank, both equal."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 238.76 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f28e25c7-cafb-404e-b234-fc1fd30a04fe")
	)
	(text "Heater supply 12.6 V DC 3.5 A (floating; referenced by the tube string midpoints)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 273.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3c9512cb-ac98-4a33-90b2-048dd40d52b5")
	)
	(text "U261 is clocked from W3 itself: U262 compares the winding polarity, C270/C271 + D266/D267 turn both edges into 190 kHz pulses (2 x fs) on RT/CLK, so the buck is locked to the LLC without crossing the isolation.\nCheck the RT/CLK pulse requirements (amplitude, width) in the TPS54560B data sheet. Heater string midpoints stay grounded at the tubes (amp sheet)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.46 360.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a30f4c1a-8852-42de-98e4-c6aac9324503")
	)
